course: dictionary
lesson: 3038
title: Earn: getting what you deserve
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To earn means to get something because you did work for it or deserved it. «Kieran still thought being the hardest kid on the street earned respect.» Kieran thinks being tough earns respect, but the context shows what really earns it: effort, skill, honesty, kindness and courage.
explain: Earn most often means getting money for work. If you do jobs at home and are paid for each one, you earn money. Your earnings are the total you get, which is the rate times the time or number of jobs.
explain: Earn can also mean getting something good you deserve, like points, praise or a badge. Money in a bank can earn interest too, which means the bank pays extra for keeping your money there.
fact: To earn means to get money because you did work.
fact: Earnings can be worked out with rate × time: £3 an hour for 4 hours means you earn £12.
fact: To earn is also to get something good because you deserve it, like points, praise or a badge.
fact: Money in a bank can earn interest.
fact: The phrase «earn a living» means to get enough money from your work to live on.
exercise: Mia does jobs at home and is paid £4 an hour for 3 hours. How much does she earn? | £3 | £43 | £7 | *£12
exercise: «Respect is earned by effort, skill, honesty, kindness and courage.» What earns respect? | Shouting the loudest | Being the hardest kid on the street | Owning the most expensive trainers | *Effort, skill, honesty, kindness and courage
exercise: Leo gets a badge for helping everyone in class. What does earned mean in «Leo earned the badge»? | He found it on the floor | He bought it in a shop | He lost it | *He got it because he deserved it
test: What does it mean to earn money? | *To get money because you did work | To lend money to a friend | To spend money on treats | To lose money in a game
test: «The bank will earn interest on your savings.» What does earn mean here? | To count coins | To give money away | To lose money | *To get extra money for keeping savings there
exam: Kieran thinks being the hardest kid on the street earns respect. According to the sentence about what earns respect, what is the better answer? | *Effort, skill, honesty, kindness and courage | Shouting the loudest | Being the hardest kid | Having the biggest bike
